### Why the required lifecycle was not converted into a pass

The native menu event is owned by the real tray runtime and is not exposed as a callable product
IPC endpoint. The only available UI paths were blocked by this session's desktop-input/API
restriction. Sending a unit event, injecting a fake menu event, using a manual helper as the
Restart/Exit action, or treating the cleanup Stop probe as tray Exit would violate the acceptance
contract, so Restart, Exit, process-survival, session rotation, and post-Exit logon semantics are
recorded as FAIL/unobserved.

