- **FAIL — Start/Heartbeat Ack evidence:** Production diagnostic files headers only; `pktmon` access denied. Remote AF_PACKET capture (65,535-byte buffer) observed continuous audio (session `1787424119882` then `1787424682907`); no Restart/Exit control packets correlated with automation attempts.
- **PASS — cleanup Stop Ack only:** Forced `Stop-Process` + explicit UDP Stop packet (session `1787424682907`) received 11-byte Stop Ack; Linux capture went `IDLE`→`SUSPENDED`, `parec` terminated.
- **PASS — safe final state:** Client process absent, task `Ready`/enabled, Linux service active, UDP listener active, no `parec`, capture source `SUSPENDED`. No firewall rules, packet filters, helper processes, or injected assemblies remain.

### Why the required lifecycle was not converted into a pass (second retry)

The `tray-icon`/`muda` crate's hidden message-only window (parent `HWND_MESSAGE`) is invisible to `EnumWindows`/`EnumThreadWindows`. The UIA overflow flyout icon's `InvokePattern` performs a left-click, which the crate does not interpret as a context-menu trigger. Without the native right-click protocol (or an IPC test seam), the real Restart/Exit menu items cannot be reached. All three escalating methods were exercised and technically failed with evidence. No unit mock, fake event, or synthetic session ID was substituted.

Todo 21 remains **UNCHECKED**.
